  <h2 class="sh">The platform</h2>
  <p class="pitch">A production autonomous agent system in Python that I built to work
    alongside me across my client book. Postgres with pgvector semantic memory, deterministic
    compliance gates, database-backed kill switches, and a completion gate that requires
    evidence before a task can be called done.</p>
  <p class="limits">It does not run the operation. It plays critical support, and it extends
    what I can deliver. Client email is draft-only except the weekly performance report, which
    auto-sends only when I arm it. Monthly reports need a manual confirm before release. Client
    ad budget, bid and copy changes are blocked outright. One account has a narrow,
    kill-switched autopilot that can only pause spend, never raise it. Stating the limits is
    what makes the rest credible.</p>
  <p class="row"><span class="k">scale</span><span>{{ metrics.metrics.python_lines.value | commas }}
    lines of Python in the repo, tests included, over 110 scheduled jobs,
    {{ metrics.metrics.agent_roles.value }} agent roles</span></p>
  <p class="row"><span class="k">measured</span><span>as of {{ metrics.snapshot }}, derived
    from the repository rather than typed by hand</span></p>

  <h2 class="sh">Results</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>101% ROI</b> on a $76,279 channel mix for a retail electricity provider, October
      2025. $153,610 revenue and 594 enrollments, closed customers rather than leads, at a
      blended cost of $128.45 each, measured through an attribution model I built.</li>
    <li><b>$253 to $38 cost per conversion</b> after launching paid search from zero for an
      at-home health testing e-commerce brand, monthly conversions from single digits to 39.</li>
    <li><b>Two Google Ads conversion actions at zero</b> for their entire lifetime on that same
      retail electricity account, so bidding was optimizing toward a signal that didn't exist.
      I built the uploader that fixed it: 194 of 197 accepted, $48,570 in conversion value.</li>
    <li><b>42.6% conversion rate</b> on the stronger of two rebuilt paid landing page variants,
      against 23.3% on the other.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="quiet">Clients anonymized by agreement. Every figure traces to a named system of record.</p>

